Notebook[{Cell["Generic Unequal-Charge Solution through O(j)", "Title"], 
  Cell["Version-3 human notation guide (documentation only; no Input cell is \
changed). In the compact solution and verifier notebooks: x=r^2; q1,q2,q3 are \
the harmonic parameters mu1,mu2,mu3, not normalized conserved charges; jrot \
is the rotation parameter j; U1,U2,U3 are the electric corrections delta u_I; \
B1,B2,B3 are the gauge-covariant fibre corrections; Om is delta omega; Ft, \
Gr, and Sq are the temporal warp, radial warp, and squashing corrections; P \
and S are delta p and delta s, where X1=exp(2p/3-s), X2=exp(2p/3+s), and \
X3=exp(-4p/3). Physical quantities are Q_I=Pi mu_I/(4 G5) and J1=J2=Pi j/(4 \
G5). See the report section 'Human-readable notation and result at a glance' \
for the full dictionary.", "Text"], Cell["Inheritance: notebooks 00-03 \
construct and reduce the equations; notebooks 04-05 validate the equal-charge \
benchmark. This notebook embeds the generic unequal-charge rational solution \
and its complete order-j residual ledger. Notebook 12 is the final literal \
from-EOM verifier.", "Text"], Cell["1. Embedded exact rational solution", 
   "Section"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"genericOrderJSolutionEvidence", "=", 
      RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", RowBox[
         {RowBox[{"\"Status\"", "\[Rule]", "\"EXACT_GENERIC_SOLUTION\""}], 
          ",", RowBox[{"\"Solution\"", "\[Rule]", 
            RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"Gauge\"", 
                  "\[Rule]", "\"dhr=0; fixed Page charges; fixed angular \
first-integral constant\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"OrderInRotation\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "1"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"b11\"", "\[Rule]", RowBox[
                   {"-", FractionBox[RowBox[{"2", " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[
